<%# Generic L4 audit-trail gate rules — language-neutral, overlay-parametrized (#1156). %>
# Audit-Trail Gate Rules — <%= industryOverlay.toUpperCase() %> overlay

> Checkable rules for the **<%= industryOverlay %>** audit-trail overlay on project
> **<%= projectName %>** (governance **<%= governanceLevel %>**). These rules are
> framework-agnostic — adapt the evidence column to your stack's audit
> implementation. Each rule is PASS/FAIL; a failing rule blocks an L4 release.

| Rule    | Statement                                                                 | Evidence to produce                                  |
| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| AUD-01  | Every governed write path emits exactly one audit record.                 | Coverage report mapping write paths → audit emitters |
| AUD-02  | Audit records are append-only (no UPDATE/DELETE on the audit store).      | Schema/permission proof; migration review            |
| AUD-03  | `actor` is always a resolved, non-anonymous identity.                     | Test asserting rejection of anonymous mutation       |
| AUD-04  | `timestamp` is server-assigned UTC; client values are ignored.            | Test asserting client timestamp is overridden        |
| AUD-05  | Records are integrity-protected (hash chain or signed).                   | Integrity-verification test over a sample chain      |
| AUD-06  | Retention window is enforced and documented.                              | Retention config + purge-after-window test           |
| AUD-07  | Audit export is reproducible and complete for any time range.             | Export round-trip test                               |

## Applying these rules

These rules are the L4 audit-trail Definition of Done for the
**<%= industryOverlay %>** overlay. They are intentionally implementation-neutral:
the pharma overlay satisfies them via JPA `AuditEvent` + ArchUnit rules, while a
generic project satisfies them with whatever audit store and tests fit its stack.
